Emacsvox News -- History Of User-Visible Changes

Maintained by Emacsvox Contributors.

* Emacsvox Unreleased --- Current User-Visible Changes

Released notes are preserved in [[file:NEWS-2026.10.0][NEWS for Emacsvox 2026.10.0]].

** Omnivox 1.18.0

The supported Omnivox baseline is now 1.18.0. This release supplies richer
tones, including waveforms, pulse width, pitch sweeps, envelopes and individual
gain. Guided installers pin the matching core and optional engines; Debian
packages recommend Omnivox 1.18.0 or newer. Updating Emacsvox does not upgrade
an existing Omnivox installation.

** Shared table reading settings

=C-e H s T= or =M-x emacsvox-table-settings= opens Tables for Markdown,
Org, Agent Shell and supported application lists. Browse pending choices,
preview with Space, then Apply to the buffer or Save common/mode defaults
through Customize. Existing Agent Shell choices retain their scope.

Plain Up/Down reads rows by default, with an optional cell setting.
Control-Meta arrows enter reading and read cells across these integrations.
Choose automatic or on-demand activation; defaults remain automatic for Agent
Shell and on demand elsewhere. =q= leaves reading in place until explicit
re-entry or leaving and returning. Render updates do not undo that quit.
Optional coordinates, brief entry, title repetition and edge behaviour retain
existing defaults. Org editing and application action keys stay independent.

** Spelling feedback

=C-e H s f= opens global spelling feedback settings. Combine voice changes,
tones and earcons independently; adjust tone pitch and duration, preview a
tone or a sample sentence, and save through Customize. The volume control
affects all main-stream tones.

Reading words marked by Flyspell places selected cues at those words instead
of after the line. Opening a mail reply retains spelling highlights without
playing a burst of cues. Repeated automatic checks announce each error once
per checking pass, while ordinary editing retains spelling feedback.

** Experimental Emacsvox menu

On the =ui-experiments= branch, =C-e H= opens a Transient. Press =s= for
Speech settings, then =i= for the existing Indentation menu. The menus share
the current-buffer or global-defaults selection; =C-u C-e H= starts with
global defaults. =C-e d I= still opens Indentation directly.

=x= opens Feedback for the captured source item; =q= there returns to the
menu with its original item and settings scope. Help also returns to its
menu with =q=. =h= opens the existing
Aural Home with all its actions; it also remains available through
=M-x emacsvox-aural=. Existing Home shortcuts follow =C-e H h= in this
prototype. =q= returns one menu, and =C-q= closes the menu sequence.
Transient feedback interrupts previous main-stream speech, including scope
toggles and value changes. Item announcements speak the key without the
word "shortcut" and do not repeat the section name.

=C-e H s n= opens Menu navigation. Choose Continuous, Wrap within section,
or Stop at section edges. Left/right moves between sections in every style.
The choice applies globally and immediately; =S= saves it through Customize.
Enter activates the focused item in the Emacsvox settings menus; =M-RET=
and =C-j= also work.

** Clear permission choice speech in Agent Shell

Tab and Shift-Tab speak each permission choice once. The cursor hint remains
visible in the echo area without speaking over the choice on the notification
stream. Other notifications remain audible.

** Indentation presentation and timing

Arkadiusz Świętnicki proposed and implemented playing indentation tones
alongside speech in [[https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox/pull/9][pull request #9]]. His idea and implementation form the
basis of this change. Alongside-speech timing is now the default on supporting
backends, with before-speech timing available as an option.

=C-e d I= opens a Transient to choose spoken or tonal indentation, tone timing,
and main-stream tone volume. Use =g= to switch between current-buffer settings
and global defaults, or open with =C-u C-e d I= to start with global defaults.
=SPC= previews the settings, and =S= saves global defaults across sessions.
Tone volume is global in either scope. Volume adjustments speak just the
percentage and interrupt previous main-stream speech. Existing direct selector commands
remain available, and spoken-only indentation feedback is unchanged.

** Announce the destination after closing an Agent Shell buffer

Closing a buffer now waits for related buffer cleanup before announcing the
newly selected buffer. This prevents Agent Shell cleanup from speaking the
name of the buffer being closed. Cancelled kills do not announce a close.
